#4471 was filed as one known parser bug. The reports merged into it have two causes.

A day-first tenant on the shared parser is the parser cause: the parser reads the month first. A day-first tenant who sent the report through the booking-v3 form is the hint cause: that form prints MM/DD/YYYY, the person types the month first, and the form reads the day first.

<Callout kind="warn">
Each cause needs a ticket of its own. The table computes the counts.
</Callout>

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Some parser reports were read as a one-day move. They stay filed under parser. The table footnotes them.

## What engineering did

#4471 closed on 5 October. The parser fix is `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The hint will not be fixed: the booking-v3 form was retired.

